{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260523230759a0c7b0fbab9243b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The IDE opened as a GUI app, which won't work for CLI mode. The Douyin DevTools doesn't seem to have a simple CLI mode like WeChat DevTools does.\n\nLet me try a different approach. Since:\n1. The CLI tools need login/cookies\n2. The API needs authentication\n3. The IDE is GUI-based\n4. We have AppID + AppSecret but not proper client_key\n\nLet me think about what other approaches we can take:\n1. **Try to use the Douyin Open Platform API with the correct parameters** - We might need to find the correct client_key (different from appid)\n2. **Try to use Playwright to automate the upload via the web console** - The踩坑记录 mentions Playwright\n3. **Try to package and upload via direct API call** using the session from the web console\n4. **Try the tmg CLI with the phone login flow** - but this needs interactive verification\n\nLet me check if there's a way to get the client_key from the platform, or try the Playwright approach since it was mentioned in the踩坑记录.\n\nActually, let me look at this from the API perspective. The `developer.toutiao.com` APIs are what the CLI tools use internally. If I can figure out the right authentication flow, I can make direct API calls.\n\nFor the toutiao developer platform:\n- The login endpoint is probably something like `developer.toutiao.com/passport/`\n- After login, cookies are stored in `~/.tmg-cli/.cookies`\n\nLet me try to see if we can use the phone + verification code approach programmatically.\n\nActually, let me look at the踩坑记录 again:\n- 发送验证码 API: `developer.toutiao.com/passport/web/send_code/`（参数: type=24, mobile=手机号, User-Agent: bytedanceide）\n- We have the user's phone: 18108431035\n\nLet me try to:\n1. Send a verification code to the user's phone\n2. Wait... but we can't interactively get the verification code since this is non-interactive mode\n\nThe踩坑记录 also mentions Playwright CDP connection to the user's Edge browser. Let me check if there's an active Edge session we can connect to.\n\nActually, the user is running this non-interactively. We can't:\n1. Get verification codes\n2. Answer interactive prompts\n3. Use GUI tools\n\nBut we CAN:\n1. Make API calls\n2. Check existing browser sessions/cookies\n3. Use Playwright for automation\n\nLet me try the Playwright approach to see if we can connect to an existing Edge browser session and use its authentication to upload.\n\nActually wait - let me re-read the task description more carefully. It says to try using the open-douyin API to get a token. Let me check the Douyin Open Platform documentation for the correct way to get an access token for mini-games.\n\nThe Douyin Open Platform has these API endpoints for OAuth:\n1. `https://open.douyin.com/oauth/connect/` - Authorization URL\n2. `https://open.douyin.com/oauth/access_token/` - Get access token\n3. `https://open.douyin.com/oauth/client_token/` - Client credentials\n\nFor client_token, the parameters should be:\n- client_key: This is NOT the appid. It's a separate key from the developer console.\n- client_secret: This is the secret\n\nBut we only have the appid and appsecret, not the client_key. The client_key is typically generated from the developer console's \"开发设置\" (Development Settings) page.\n\nHmm, this is tricky. Let me try another approach.\n\nActually, let me check if there's a way to get the client_key using the API. Or maybe the appid IS the client_key for some platforms.\n\nWait, for the toutiao developer platform (not open-douyin), the API might work differently. Let me try:\n```\nPOST https://developer.toutiao.com/api/v2/token\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n    \"appid\": \"tte7a1911c79c6fc8302\",\n    \"secret\": \"1e84b6c01d7906704f6bf4caf104b193334abb49\",\n    \"grant_type\": \"client_credential\"\n}\n```\n\nEarlier this returned \"当前未登录\" (not logged in). But maybe we need different headers.\n\nActually, looking at the toutiao developer API documentation, the `/api/v2/token` endpoint should work with appid+secret without needing cookies. The fact that it returned \"not logged in\" might be because:\n1. The appid format is wrong\n2. The API endpoint is different for mini-games\n3. The secret is for a different API\n\nLet me try using the mini-game specific token endpoint. For Douyin mini-games, the token endpoint might be:\n```\nPOST https://developer.toutiao.com/api/apps/token\n```\n\nOr maybe the issue is that the appid starts with \"tte\" which is a mini-program prefix, and for mini-games it should be different.\n\nLet me try a few more API approaches, and if none work, I'll try the Playwright/CDP approach to connect to the user's browser.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33adb7f4-913e-4960-83b6-3354bfda46a0","uuid":"c001a5dd-6f33-453f-8aa0-4ca796c02f07"}
