{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260523231519a5ff7a10134d4cd5","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The token is stored in the appConfig.json. But the CLI says \"not logged in\". Let me look at this more carefully.\n\nThe cookies in `.tma-cli/.cookies` have `_dy_open` suffix cookies, which are from the open-douyin.com platform. The tma CLI likely needs cookies from `developer.toutiao.com` without the `_dy_open` suffix.\n\nLet me check if there are cookies from `developer.toutiao.com` (without the `_dy_open` suffix). Looking at the cookie string again:\n- `sid_tt_dy_open` - open platform\n- `sessionid_dy_open` - open platform\n- No plain `sid_tt` or `sessionid` without the suffix\n\nSo the cookies are from the open-douyin.com platform, not the toutiao.com developer platform. That's why the CLI says \"not logged in\".\n\nThe `tma set-app-config` stored the token, but the CLI still checks for a valid session first. Let me check the tma source code to understand the authentication flow.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach. Let me check if there's a way to use the `tmg` CLI (which is specifically for mini-games) instead. But first, let me check if tmg has cookies.\n\nWait, actually, let me re-read the config. The tma config has these URLs:\n- `upload`: `https://developer.toutiao.com/api/v2/app/${appid}/testing`\n- But there's also `interactGameUrl.upload`: `https://developer.toutiao.com/api/developer/ide/v1/testing`\n- And `microgameUrl.upload`: `https://developer.toutiao.com/api/developer/ide/microgame/v1/testing?appid=`\n\nSo depending on the project type, different upload URLs are used. For miniapp, it uses `/api/v2/app/${appid}/testing`. For microgame, it uses `/api/developer/ide/microgame/v1/testing`.\n\nThe session validation might check the cookies against the correct domain. Since our cookies have `_dy_open` suffix, they're from the open-douyin.com domain. But the API calls go to `devel