{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026052323195335e26c1d4f9a4e1f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The page shows \"网站升级中\" (Website Under Maintenance/Upgrade) and \"当前页面不存在，即将回到首页\" (The current page does not exist; returning to the homepage soon). This matches what the踩坑记录 said: \"新版控制台游戏管理页（`console/miniapp/{appId}/version`）显示'网站升级中'，不可用\".\n\nBut wait - the screenshot shows the user IS logged in (username \"uunderli...\" is visible in the top right). So the cookies work for authentication, but the version management page itself is under maintenance/unavailable.\n\nThe踩坑记录 also says:\n- \"正确的游戏管理入口: `/game-console/1065926/game-manage`（从HTML中提取的href）\"\n\nBut the AppID is for a mini-program, not a game. Let me try the mini-program console instead.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The page `/console/miniapp/${APPID}/version` shows \"网站升级中\". This means the mini-program version management page is not available through this URL.\n\nLet me check if there's a different URL for the mini-program version management. Maybe:\n1. `/console/miniapp/${APPID}/` - main mini-app console\n2. Or the old-style URL format\n\nLet me try navigating to the mini-program management page and see what's available.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach entirely. Instead of the web console, let me try to make the CLI work. The issue with the CLI was authentication. The cookies in `.tma-cli/.cookies` are from the open-douyin.com platform, but the CLI needs cookies from `developer.toutiao.com`.\n\nWhat if I can translate the cookies? The session IDs should be the same across platforms since they're all under the ByteDance ecosystem. Let me try modifying the cookies to work with the toutiao.com domain by removing the `_dy_open` suffix.\n\nActually, that probably won't work because the domain binding is different. Let me try yet another approach.\n\nThe tma CLI has a `login-e` command for email login. The user's email is `1163155015@qq.com`. But we don't have the password.\n\nWait - what if I can use the `tmg` CLI instead of `tma`? The `tmg` CLI is specifically for mini-games. Let me check if `tmg` has the same authentication requirements.\n\nActually, looking at the CLI config again:\n- `tma` stores cookies in `~/.tma-cli/.cookies`\n- `tmg` stores cookies in `~/.tmg-cli/.cookies`\n\nThe tmg cookies might be different. Let me check if tmg has any cookies stored.\n\nBut earlier we checked and tmg had no cookies. Let me try to get the tmg CLI to use the same cookies from tma.\n\nActually, let me try something else. Let me try to use the email login approach with the tma CLI. Maybe I can pipe the output and see what happens. But we don't have the password...\n\nLet me try another approach. The open-douyin.com API might have an upload endpoint for mini-programs. Let me search for the correct API.\n\nActually, let me check if the Douyin Open Platform has a REST API for uploading mini-program code. The standard flow is:\n1. Get access_token using client_key and client_secret\n2. Use the upload API with the access_token\n\nBut we only have the AppID and AppSecret, not the client_key. The client_key is generated separately from the developer console.\n\nWait - let me check if the AppSecret IS actually the client_secret for the open platform. Let me try different parameter names in the API call.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33adb7f4-913e-4960-83b6-3354bfda46a0","uuid":"4dce0e5f-e8ad-4b31-9a5b-951379d58d1e"}
